# Commit everything when asked

When the user asks to **commit** (or commit and push):

- Stage **all** modified and untracked project files that belong in git — do not leave related leftovers out of the commit to keep the message “focused.”
- Do not selectively omit scripts, assets, tools, `.cursor/rules`, launchers, or docs that are part of the current working tree unless they are secrets (`.env`, credentials) or clearly machine-local junk (build caches, `.godot/` imports, personal notes outside the repo).
- If changes span multiple concerns, prefer **one commit with a message that covers them**, or multiple commits that **together** clear the working tree — never finish with intentional uncommitted project files after a commit request.
- Still follow the usual git safety rules (no force-push to main, no amend unless allowed, no secrets).
